WEBVTT

1
00:01:25.210 --> 00:01:27.795
(SUSPENSEFUL MUSIC)

2
00:01:48.858 --> 00:01:50.567
(SNARLING)

3
00:01:51.277 --> 00:01:52.778
MAN: Hyperion!

4
00:02:09.087 --> 00:02:11.338
(PANTING, GASPING)

5
00:02:34.195 --> 00:02:36.321
(SPEAKING FOREIGN LANGUAGE)

6
00:03:13.735 --> 00:03:16.445
MAN: When this world was still young...

7
00:03:18.615 --> 00:03:22.534
...long before man or beast
roamed these lands...

8
00:03:26.873 --> 00:03:29.208
...there was a war in the heavens.

9
00:03:31.211 --> 00:03:35.380
Immortals, once thought
incapable of death...

10
00:03:36.299 --> 00:03:39.301
...discovered they had the power
to kill one another.

11
00:03:40.511 --> 00:03:45.599
Lost in this war was a weapon
of unimaginable power:

12
00:03:46.476 --> 00:03:48.101
the Epirus Bow.

13
00:03:49.604 --> 00:03:53.232
The victors declared themselves gods

14
00:03:53.399 --> 00:03:57.361
while the vanquished
were renamed Titans,

15
00:03:57.528 --> 00:04:01.657
and forever imprisoned
within the bowels of Mount Tartarus.

16
00:04:03.117 --> 00:04:07.788
Eons passed. Mankind flourished.

17
00:04:07.956 --> 00:04:10.791
And the great war receded from memory.

18
00:04:14.545 --> 00:04:16.755
But the evil that once was...

19
00:04:21.344 --> 00:04:23.095
...has re-emerged.

20
00:04:23.263 --> 00:04:25.639
(CROWD SHOUTING)

21
00:04:33.398 --> 00:04:35.983
(SPEAKING FOREIGN LANGUAGE)

22
00:04:53.543 --> 00:04:56.253
(MULTIPLE FOOTSTEPS
RAPIDLY APPROACHING)

23
00:05:04.470 --> 00:05:07.306
Stop. You cannot enter here.
This is sacred ground.

24
00:05:08.349 --> 00:05:09.808
Sacred for who?

25
00:05:11.686 --> 00:05:13.020
What do you want with us?

26
00:05:14.522 --> 00:05:16.231
Where is the virgin oracle?

27
00:05:20.403 --> 00:05:24.448
Defile this house further
and you will risk the wrath of the gods.

28
00:05:28.077 --> 00:05:29.411
The gods?

29
00:05:32.165 --> 00:05:35.083
(SPITS) Gods.

30
00:05:37.337 --> 00:05:38.503
Gods.

31
00:05:40.131 --> 00:05:41.673
Go ahead, call upon them.

32
00:05:42.633 --> 00:05:45.927
Pray. Ask for their help.

33
00:05:47.847 --> 00:05:51.808
Pray to the same gods
who idly stood by...

34
00:05:52.852 --> 00:05:57.064
...as my wife and my children
were stricken by disease.

35
00:05:58.524 --> 00:06:00.734
I, too, cried to the heavens for help.

36
00:06:03.988 --> 00:06:08.784
But instead of mercy,
I was met with silence.

37
00:06:08.951 --> 00:06:11.328
And the wretched sight of my family...

38
00:06:12.205 --> 00:06:15.707
...suffering like animals
untiI their deaths.

39
00:06:17.043 --> 00:06:18.543
Your gods will no longer mock me.

40
00:06:18.711 --> 00:06:20.295
(CUP CLATTERS)

41
00:06:23.299 --> 00:06:24.758
I will release the Titans.

42
00:06:24.926 --> 00:06:27.552
It's not too late to end this madness.

43
00:06:27.720 --> 00:06:30.222
Salvation can be yours, if you wish it.

44
00:06:32.058 --> 00:06:34.226
Let me enlighten you, priest.

45
00:06:38.272 --> 00:06:40.440
(SCREAMING)

46
00:06:42.068 --> 00:06:43.985
I will end the reign of gods.

47
00:06:59.335 --> 00:07:01.795
You wield that ax well, Theseus.

48
00:07:02.880 --> 00:07:07.259
Maybe someday we'll see you use
the same determination to find a wife.

49
00:07:08.511 --> 00:07:10.220
Are you conspiring with my mother now?

50
00:07:10.638 --> 00:07:11.972
She worries about you.

51
00:07:12.682 --> 00:07:14.182
There's no need to worry about me.

52
00:07:15.184 --> 00:07:16.935
You know, being a warrior...

53
00:07:18.104 --> 00:07:21.857
...is notjust being able to strike
your opponent down with a sword.

54
00:07:22.024 --> 00:07:26.736
It's finding good reason
to draw your sword in the first place.

55
00:07:27.655 --> 00:07:29.781
I draw my sword
to protect those that I love.

56
00:07:30.950 --> 00:07:32.284
What about the others?

57
00:07:32.952 --> 00:07:35.579
- The others turn their backs on me.
- The weak?

58
00:07:35.746 --> 00:07:38.790
The defenseless?
Who's going to protect them?

59
00:07:38.958 --> 00:07:40.542
(SCOFFS)

60
00:07:42.879 --> 00:07:45.881
CarefuI. Too much worrying
will make you an old man.

61
00:07:57.810 --> 00:07:58.810
- Whore.
- Oh!

62
00:08:00.396 --> 00:08:02.063
MAN: Last lights for the labyrinth.

63
00:08:03.733 --> 00:08:05.901
Last lights for the holy labyrinth.

64
00:08:10.490 --> 00:08:12.824
Let the ancestors rest in peace.

65
00:08:25.171 --> 00:08:27.005
(COOING)

66
00:08:34.889 --> 00:08:36.473
(WHISPERS) Theseus...

67
00:08:37.808 --> 00:08:39.434
MAN: May the gods be with you.

68
00:08:41.103 --> 00:08:42.938
Thank you for the offerings.

69
00:08:43.105 --> 00:08:44.439
Another accident?

70
00:08:47.276 --> 00:08:51.988
Theseus. Maybe one day
you'll join me in prayer.

71
00:08:52.156 --> 00:08:54.783
Ask the gods to grant me grandchildren
before I'm too old.

72
00:08:54.951 --> 00:08:59.329
Mother, your gods are children's
stories. My spear is not.

73
00:09:00.665 --> 00:09:04.209
And you know, Mother, it takes more
than lighting candles to make babies.

74
00:09:04.377 --> 00:09:05.460
(MOTHER CHUCKLES)

75
00:09:05.628 --> 00:09:08.421
THESEUS: Besides, our priest
wears a ridiculous hat.

76
00:09:09.465 --> 00:09:10.465
MOTHER: Theseus.

77
00:09:13.052 --> 00:09:14.553
(SEAGULLS CRYING)

78
00:09:33.155 --> 00:09:35.824
(GONG CONTINUES)

79
00:09:44.250 --> 00:09:45.375
Mother, stay here.

80
00:09:45.543 --> 00:09:46.876
Theseus.

81
00:10:07.273 --> 00:10:09.232
MAN: Fellow Hellenics!

82
00:10:09.400 --> 00:10:11.860
It is with great concern
that I stand before you.

83
00:10:12.778 --> 00:10:17.282
The Heraklion king, Hyperion,
has seized the Sibylline Monastery.

84
00:10:17.450 --> 00:10:18.450
(CROWD SHOUTING)

85
00:10:18.618 --> 00:10:20.910
He is only a day's march from here.

86
00:10:21.078 --> 00:10:24.039
We must evacuate
this village immediately.

87
00:10:24.206 --> 00:10:25.874
We must fight him
at the gates of our village!

88
00:10:26.042 --> 00:10:28.376
Silence, please! Quiet!

89
00:10:28.544 --> 00:10:30.045
MAN: Villagers, we stand no chance!

90
00:10:30.212 --> 00:10:33.256
- I said fall in, Lysander!
- We stand no chance!

91
00:10:33.424 --> 00:10:35.050
He is weary from battle!

92
00:10:35.217 --> 00:10:39.929
Please. We ask that every man, woman
and child gather your belongings.

93
00:10:40.097 --> 00:10:41.723
Leave for Mount Tartarus.

94
00:10:42.475 --> 00:10:45.644
Seek refuge behind the safety
of the great wall!

95
00:10:45.811 --> 00:10:47.520
There you will be protected.

96
00:10:47.688 --> 00:10:50.899
Anyone who needs more time,
the old, the infirm,

97
00:10:51.067 --> 00:10:52.776
we will escort in a day's time.

98
00:10:52.943 --> 00:10:55.320
- Only what you can carry.
- MAN: Prepare your departure.

99
00:10:55.488 --> 00:10:58.073
Leave it. It's not essentiaI.
Give me that.

100
00:11:00.326 --> 00:11:02.118
- Leave that.
- (ANIMAL SOUNDS)

101
00:11:03.329 --> 00:11:04.454
MAN 2: Move along now.

102
00:11:04.830 --> 00:11:06.164
You're with the wrong party.

103
00:11:07.917 --> 00:11:09.584
Is this not the caravan
traveling to Tartarus?

104
00:11:09.752 --> 00:11:12.170
It is, but you will not
be traveling among us.

105
00:11:13.214 --> 00:11:14.881
Go in the morning with your own kind.

106
00:11:15.591 --> 00:11:16.758
My kind?

107
00:11:17.760 --> 00:11:20.428
Peasants and undesirables
traveI tomorrow.

108
00:11:22.598 --> 00:11:24.683
My kind's blood
is the same color as yours.

109
00:11:24.850 --> 00:11:26.351
- Should we spill some to prove it?
- Theseus.

110
00:11:26.519 --> 00:11:27.686
Mother.

111
00:11:27.853 --> 00:11:29.354
What happens here?

112
00:11:30.523 --> 00:11:32.524
This bastard and his whore mother...

113
00:11:32.692 --> 00:11:34.234
(GRUNTING)

114
00:11:41.951 --> 00:11:44.369
Stop! Fall back!

115
00:11:46.122 --> 00:11:47.497
Fall back!

116
00:11:51.127 --> 00:11:52.460
- Put the sword down.
- I will not!

117
00:11:52.628 --> 00:11:55.213
- Kill him!
- Try! He dies first.

118
00:11:56.215 --> 00:11:58.049
What is it that you want, brother?

119
00:11:58.217 --> 00:12:01.594
It seems as though my kind
traveI in the morning.

120
00:12:02.430 --> 00:12:03.888
I want them to have a proper escort.

121
00:12:04.056 --> 00:12:05.849
(BOTH SHOUT)

122
00:12:08.310 --> 00:12:11.438
Move again, and I will bury this
in your skull.

123
00:12:12.606 --> 00:12:14.983
- What's your name?
- Theseus.

124
00:12:15.151 --> 00:12:18.153
Now is not the time
for violence, Theseus. Let him go.

125
00:12:19.155 --> 00:12:22.157
Only if I have your word the rest
of the village will be protected.

126
00:12:22.324 --> 00:12:26.578
You have my word. I will leave
capable men for the caravan tomorrow.

127
00:12:30.541 --> 00:12:32.876
- Kill this traitor!
- Enough with your spectacle!

128
00:12:33.043 --> 00:12:35.503
Restrain him! Get him out of my sight!

129
00:12:35.671 --> 00:12:37.255
MAN: He's a bastard!

130
00:12:37.423 --> 00:12:39.299
MAN 2: Take him away and disarm him.

131
00:12:39.467 --> 00:12:40.467
Mother...

132
00:12:42.094 --> 00:12:45.180
Save your bloodlust
for Heraklion veins, Theseus.

133
00:12:45.347 --> 00:12:49.100
Join our ranks.
You have been trained well.

134
00:12:51.854 --> 00:12:53.354
I had a good teacher.

135
00:12:53.522 --> 00:12:56.858
I could use men of your skill at our
side to defeat Hyperion's legions.

136
00:12:57.026 --> 00:13:01.446
Why would I serve you?
You who would so easily abandon us.

137
00:13:02.531 --> 00:13:03.948
Let's go, Mother.

138
00:13:09.622 --> 00:13:13.625
Lysander. You're no longer
part of this army.

139
00:13:16.337 --> 00:13:19.047
Relinquish your shield, your spear...

140
00:13:20.216 --> 00:13:22.300
...and remain here to traveI
with the peasants tomorrow.

141
00:13:22.468 --> 00:13:24.302
- But you saw him...
- It's done.

142
00:13:31.143 --> 00:13:32.477
I'll see you later.

143
00:13:36.482 --> 00:13:40.401
Where are your things, old man?
Are you not prepared for the march?

144
00:13:41.987 --> 00:13:45.907
Such odysseys were meant
for the young and expectant,

145
00:13:46.075 --> 00:13:48.493
not for a worn-out old goat like me.

146
00:13:49.161 --> 00:13:52.747
Please reconsider.
You know staying here is suicide.

147
00:13:53.999 --> 00:13:58.253
If the Heraklions show up,
at least I'll be spared a slow death.

148
00:13:58.420 --> 00:14:03.383
From what I understand,
indecision is not their style.

149
00:14:04.927 --> 00:14:06.135
You are mad.

150
00:14:06.303 --> 00:14:07.512
(CHUCKLES) No.

151
00:14:08.931 --> 00:14:10.306
Just tired.

152
00:14:12.601 --> 00:14:17.188
It's not living as such
that's important, Theseus.

153
00:14:18.023 --> 00:14:19.774
It's living rightly.

154
00:14:26.574 --> 00:14:29.117
They fight with a ferocity
unlike anything I've seen.

155
00:14:31.036 --> 00:14:33.454
It was as if they could
see in the darkness.

156
00:14:35.207 --> 00:14:36.541
As though it suited them.

157
00:14:37.710 --> 00:14:39.377
You speak as if they're not human.

158
00:14:40.129 --> 00:14:44.173
They are human.
The Heraklions bleed just as we do.

159
00:14:45.134 --> 00:14:48.011
The only difference is
they fight for a belief

160
00:14:48.178 --> 00:14:50.889
which allows them to kill
without restraint.

161
00:14:51.682 --> 00:14:53.308
That is why they will win.

162
00:14:53.475 --> 00:14:56.978
Lysander. I thought Helios
ordered you disarmed.

163
00:14:57.730 --> 00:14:58.730
He did.

164
00:14:59.398 --> 00:15:01.065
(GRUNTING)

165
00:15:05.070 --> 00:15:08.281
(GROANING)

166
00:15:11.577 --> 00:15:13.745
(GRUTNING, PANTING)

167
00:15:13.913 --> 00:15:15.830
(SHOUTS)

168
00:15:16.916 --> 00:15:19.334
(WOLVES HOWLING)

169
00:15:37.436 --> 00:15:39.437
ReveaI yourself.

170
00:15:42.608 --> 00:15:44.692
(RUMBLING)

171
00:15:53.118 --> 00:15:54.619
ReveaI yourself.

172
00:15:59.291 --> 00:16:02.627
- Father.
- Athena.

173
00:16:11.470 --> 00:16:13.554
- Zeus.
- No need for formalities.

174
00:16:15.307 --> 00:16:18.101
None of the other gods
are looking, are they?

175
00:16:19.144 --> 00:16:20.144
(CHUCKLES)

176
00:16:21.271 --> 00:16:22.313
What?

177
00:16:22.982 --> 00:16:26.275
When you walked up here just now,
you actually looked like a father.

178
00:16:26.986 --> 00:16:28.820
Or maybe a grandfather.

179
00:16:28.988 --> 00:16:29.988
(VOICES OUTSIDE)

180
00:16:31.240 --> 00:16:34.534
We must tread carefully here.
Heed the law.

181
00:16:34.702 --> 00:16:38.162
None of the mortals on Earth
should witness us in our immortaI form.

182
00:16:38.330 --> 00:16:40.289
But, Father, you've come
dangerously close.

183
00:16:40.457 --> 00:16:43.668
You've been influencing
the boy Theseus for years.

184
00:16:43.836 --> 00:16:46.671
Yet as one of them. Never as a god.

185
00:16:46.839 --> 00:16:48.256
Only as his friend.

186
00:16:50.843 --> 00:16:52.176
And why him?

187
00:16:57.433 --> 00:16:59.183
He does not fear danger.

188
00:17:00.519 --> 00:17:04.480
Nor pain, defeat, or ridicule.

189
00:17:05.357 --> 00:17:09.527
He fears only the failure to defend
that which he holds so dear.

190
00:17:12.197 --> 00:17:13.364
His loved ones.

191
00:17:14.533 --> 00:17:17.869
If there is one human who could
lead them against Hyperion...

192
00:17:19.538 --> 00:17:21.372
...it would be Theseus.

193
00:17:22.374 --> 00:17:24.167
But it must be his choice.

194
00:17:24.334 --> 00:17:26.461
(THUNDER RUMBLES)

195
00:17:34.845 --> 00:17:37.513
He's a defector.
He wants to meet the king.

196
00:17:38.724 --> 00:17:41.392
- (SIZZLING)
- (MUFFLED SCREAMS)

197
00:17:54.406 --> 00:17:55.698
(GRUNTS)

198
00:18:05.417 --> 00:18:07.710
(CLANKING SOUNDS)

199
00:18:27.189 --> 00:18:29.357
(MUFFLED SCREAMS)

200
00:18:51.922 --> 00:18:52.922
Move.

201
00:19:00.806 --> 00:19:02.974
(MUFFLED SCREAMS CONTINUE)

202
00:19:15.696 --> 00:19:18.614
(PANTING)

203
00:19:18.782 --> 00:19:21.284
You are a defector, I understand.

204
00:19:23.328 --> 00:19:25.788
- Yes, my king.
- I am not your king.

205
00:19:27.624 --> 00:19:30.585
But I wish you to be.

206
00:19:31.587 --> 00:19:34.338
But you are a traitor by definition,
are you not?

207
00:19:35.841 --> 00:19:39.135
What would I want
with a traitor in my midst?

208
00:19:40.762 --> 00:19:44.849
I can tell you of a village
that lies unprotected...

209
00:19:45.809 --> 00:19:49.353
- ... where you can gather young women.
- I have plenty ofwomen.

210
00:19:49.521 --> 00:19:53.441
- Slaves and weaponry.
- I have plenty ofweapons.

211
00:19:54.735 --> 00:19:57.236
What I want is the Epirus Bow.

212
00:19:58.572 --> 00:20:03.910
Like this monastery, I have moved every
precious stone your people worship upon.

213
00:20:08.415 --> 00:20:10.041
And I have yet to find it.

214
00:20:10.209 --> 00:20:11.709
(MAN MOANS)

215
00:20:18.592 --> 00:20:20.468
(PANTING)

216
00:20:26.058 --> 00:20:28.684
Have you ever met
a Sibylline monk, traitor?

217
00:20:29.853 --> 00:20:34.106
Monks of his order are unwavering
in their obedience to the virgin oracle.

218
00:20:34.858 --> 00:20:38.778
With the right prodding, the oracle
could see where the Bow rests.

219
00:20:41.740 --> 00:20:43.074
Couldn't she, monk?

220
00:20:46.411 --> 00:20:47.870
Tell me where she is.

221
00:20:58.382 --> 00:21:00.341
I know of your faith, monk.

222
00:21:02.094 --> 00:21:05.596
Sybellines are forbidden to take a life
under any circumstance...

223
00:21:06.807 --> 00:21:08.140
...even their own.

224
00:21:09.977 --> 00:21:13.104
You have no choice
but to tell me what I want to know.

225
00:21:17.192 --> 00:21:18.276
(GASPS)

226
00:21:19.486 --> 00:21:20.528
(GROANING)

227
00:21:23.365 --> 00:21:26.909
A monk can be made to talk
with or without his tongue.

228
00:21:27.869 --> 00:21:31.247
Give him to the beast. Make him tell you
where the oracle is being kept.

229
00:21:37.796 --> 00:21:39.463
Do you have any children?

230
00:21:41.133 --> 00:21:42.174
Not yet.

231
00:21:43.010 --> 00:21:46.637
A man's seed can be
his most brutaI weapon.

232
00:21:47.306 --> 00:21:52.101
For generations, your people will
stare into the eyes of their sons

233
00:21:52.269 --> 00:21:54.562
and they will see my likeness.

234
00:21:56.440 --> 00:21:59.942
I will be remembered
in every glance, every smile,

235
00:22:00.110 --> 00:22:03.321
every tear that is shed for eternity.

236
00:22:03.488 --> 00:22:07.283
But before your baptism,
understand that you are not

237
00:22:07.451 --> 00:22:11.996
drawn here to my flame on instinct.

238
00:22:15.876 --> 00:22:17.168
(WHIMPERS)

239
00:22:17.336 --> 00:22:20.546
But you ran here
because you are a coward.

240
00:22:23.675 --> 00:22:28.054
And the world does not need
any more cowards.

241
00:22:34.519 --> 00:22:37.104
So, I shall do this world a great favor.

242
00:22:37.856 --> 00:22:39.357
Mark you as one of us...

243
00:22:39.524 --> 00:22:41.567
(SCREAMS)

244
00:22:41.735 --> 00:22:46.238
...and rid you of your ability
to populate the Earth.

245
00:22:48.533 --> 00:22:50.368
- Traitor.
- (WHIMPERS)

246
00:22:50.535 --> 00:22:52.244
Although you will not hear them...

247
00:22:55.123 --> 00:22:57.708
...your forefathers weep
from their graves...

248
00:22:59.336 --> 00:23:01.504
...for the future of their bloodline...

249
00:23:04.132 --> 00:23:06.384
...ends with you here tonight.

250
00:23:08.011 --> 00:23:10.179
- (CRUNCHING SOUNDS)
- (LYSANDER SCREAMS)

251
00:23:13.225 --> 00:23:14.266
Theseus: Old Man?

252
00:23:17.938 --> 00:23:19.063
Old Man.

253
00:23:29.449 --> 00:23:30.533
Hello?

254
00:23:32.411 --> 00:23:34.078
(BIRD SCREECHES)

255
00:23:45.382 --> 00:23:48.134
(FAINT THUDDING SOUNDS)

256
00:23:49.761 --> 00:23:55.266
Your anger rules you, Theseus.
You must learn to master your emotions.

257
00:23:55.434 --> 00:23:58.144
(THESEUS GRUNTING)

258
00:23:58.311 --> 00:24:01.939
Rhythm, Theseus. Rhythm.

259
00:24:18.206 --> 00:24:20.207
(BIRD SCREECHING)

260
00:24:34.556 --> 00:24:36.765
(FIGHTING SOUNDS)

261
00:24:39.978 --> 00:24:42.396
(WOMEN SCREAMING)

262
00:24:50.655 --> 00:24:52.281
MAN: You! Burn that down!

263
00:24:55.035 --> 00:24:56.494
Get over here!

264
00:24:58.788 --> 00:25:00.831
- No!
- Huh?

265
00:25:00.999 --> 00:25:01.832
Theseus!

266
00:25:03.460 --> 00:25:05.544
(SHOUTS)

267
00:25:08.215 --> 00:25:10.549
(GRUNTING)

268
00:25:18.141 --> 00:25:20.351
(SHOUTS FIERCLY)

269
00:25:23.021 --> 00:25:24.355
(GASPS)

270
00:25:31.363 --> 00:25:33.030
(SHOUTING CONTINUES)

271
00:25:34.199 --> 00:25:37.243
- HYPERION: Wait.
- (WHIMPERING)

272
00:25:41.540 --> 00:25:43.541
- (THESEUS CONTINUES GRUNTING)
- (GASPS)

273
00:25:49.548 --> 00:25:51.757
Witness hell.

274
00:25:53.385 --> 00:25:55.594
No!

275
00:25:59.516 --> 00:26:01.267
No!

276
00:26:02.686 --> 00:26:04.311
No!

277
00:26:05.689 --> 00:26:06.689
Not him.

278
00:26:07.691 --> 00:26:08.566
No!

279
00:26:08.733 --> 00:26:12.152
Give him to the jailer.
He can work in the salt mines.

280
00:26:16.491 --> 00:26:18.576
His pain has just begun.

281
00:26:21.413 --> 00:26:23.497
(WOMEN CONTINUE SCREAMING)

282
00:26:33.091 --> 00:26:36.385
WOMAN: Hyperion's legions
show no mercy.

283
00:26:39.723 --> 00:26:44.602
They have destroyed every holy shrine
in their quest for the Epirus Bow.

284
00:26:47.689 --> 00:26:51.025
It is only a matter of time
before they find it.

285
00:26:53.028 --> 00:26:56.905
I've noticed their king
takes the greatest care

286
00:26:57.073 --> 00:26:59.408
with all women who carry a child.

287
00:27:00.493 --> 00:27:02.911
And personally sees
to their slaughter.

288
00:27:05.457 --> 00:27:08.459
He ventures to eradicate
a Hellenic future.

289
00:27:09.628 --> 00:27:11.629
They honor no rules of engagement.

290
00:27:11.796 --> 00:27:15.466
Effective. At least thus far.

291
00:27:15.634 --> 00:27:16.634
Effective?

292
00:27:18.470 --> 00:27:21.305
- Cowardly.
- That may be...

293
00:27:22.724 --> 00:27:26.310
...but the Hellenics have yet to adapt,
and untiI they do...

294
00:27:26.478 --> 00:27:28.771
Isn't it time to intervene, Zeus?

295
00:27:29.814 --> 00:27:33.150
How can you stomach bearing witness
to such atrocity whilst doing nothing?

296
00:27:33.318 --> 00:27:38.238
I obey the law. No god shall interfere
in the affairs of man

297
00:27:38.406 --> 00:27:40.616
unless the Titans are released.

298
00:27:40.784 --> 00:27:44.036
Ifwe are to expect mankind
to have faith in us,

299
00:27:44.204 --> 00:27:45.913
then we must have faith in them.

300
00:27:46.081 --> 00:27:48.624
We must allow them
to use their own free will.

301
00:27:49.334 --> 00:27:51.168
And what if they unearth the Bow?

302
00:27:57.384 --> 00:28:01.345
If any of you come to the aid of man

303
00:28:01.513 --> 00:28:05.599
or otherwise influence
the affairs of mankind as a god...

304
00:28:07.352 --> 00:28:09.186
...the punishment will be death.

305
00:29:11.458 --> 00:29:13.041
Who are they?

306
00:29:13.835 --> 00:29:17.921
The virgin oracles. The Heraklions
must have found their temple.

307
00:29:19.591 --> 00:29:22.259
- You don't know of them?
- MAN: I don't.

308
00:29:22.927 --> 00:29:24.928
I wouldn't mind knowing them all
for a night.

309
00:29:31.227 --> 00:29:32.770
(GASPS)

310
00:29:47.243 --> 00:29:50.579
(PANTING) When cloudless
skies thunder, stand fast.

311
00:30:05.762 --> 00:30:06.804
(WATER SLOSHES)

312
00:30:13.770 --> 00:30:15.103
You were a thief?

313
00:30:16.606 --> 00:30:18.315
I am a thief, my lady.

314
00:30:19.818 --> 00:30:23.028
Were it not for these chains,
I'd steaI your heart.

315
00:30:23.571 --> 00:30:25.656
Tonight we must flee this place.

316
00:30:27.784 --> 00:30:29.660
Whichever are strong enough to fight.

317
00:30:31.871 --> 00:30:33.330
And that man there.

318
00:30:33.498 --> 00:30:36.750
He didn't even go for the water.
He won't make it till morning.

319
00:30:36.918 --> 00:30:38.168
Just be ready.

320
00:31:05.780 --> 00:31:06.697
Stay apart.

321
00:31:09.951 --> 00:31:10.951
Inside.

322
00:31:13.371 --> 00:31:14.538
Stay alive.

323
00:31:29.012 --> 00:31:30.596
(WHISPERS IN FOREIGN LANGUAGE)

324
00:32:08.259 --> 00:32:12.387
Only one of them is the true oracle.
A seer. She is pure.

325
00:32:14.641 --> 00:32:16.975
The others are there
to protect her identity.

326
00:32:19.812 --> 00:32:23.607
The virgin oracle is blessed
with visions of the future.

327
00:32:25.026 --> 00:32:29.112
Were she to be violated,
her gift of prophecy would be corrupted.

328
00:32:30.657 --> 00:32:31.990
What a waste.

329
00:33:01.896 --> 00:33:03.981
- (SLICING SOUNDS)
- (MUFFLED GRUNTING)

330
00:33:09.529 --> 00:33:11.571
- Guards!
- Keys!

331
00:33:12.949 --> 00:33:14.449
(FOREIGN LANGUAGE)

332
00:33:42.812 --> 00:33:45.188
(WAVES CRASHING)

333
00:33:52.030 --> 00:33:53.405
You should get some sleep.

334
00:33:58.286 --> 00:34:00.704
Do you know, I am stronger than I look?

335
00:34:04.250 --> 00:34:05.584
I'll be fine.

336
00:34:13.009 --> 00:34:14.217
Perhaps...

337
00:34:15.553 --> 00:34:17.763
Perhaps you have
trouble sleeping because...

338
00:34:18.973 --> 00:34:20.724
...you're haunted by your visions.

339
00:34:23.561 --> 00:34:25.353
A warrior who reads minds.

340
00:34:30.735 --> 00:34:32.486
(BOTH CHUCKLE)

341
00:34:33.404 --> 00:34:37.407
Some people do consider
my visions to be a gift.

342
00:34:37.575 --> 00:34:41.453
Gift? How can it be considered a gift

343
00:34:41.621 --> 00:34:44.664
when you can see the future but you
don't have the power to change it?

344
00:34:53.091 --> 00:34:54.424
Sorry.

345
00:34:59.097 --> 00:35:00.722
Why would you do such a thing?

346
00:35:02.475 --> 00:35:05.102
You risked your life
to save a complete stranger.

347
00:35:05.937 --> 00:35:08.188
Only a faithless man
would ask such a question.

348
00:35:08.856 --> 00:35:11.608
My mother was a woman of faith

349
00:35:11.776 --> 00:35:14.402
and her gods were absent
when she needed them the most.

350
00:35:21.160 --> 00:35:22.494
As was I.

351
00:35:25.706 --> 00:35:27.541
So we both mourn.

352
00:35:29.961 --> 00:35:31.795
You for what has passed and...

353
00:35:33.589 --> 00:35:35.173
...and I for what is to come.

354
00:35:44.142 --> 00:35:46.184
(INDISTINCT SHOUTING)

355
00:36:00.825 --> 00:36:02.159
HYPERION: What happened to them?

356
00:36:06.205 --> 00:36:09.040
I gave an order
for them not to be touched.

357
00:36:09.208 --> 00:36:11.585
MAN: They tried to flee, my king.

358
00:36:11.752 --> 00:36:14.212
Seven of our best men
were killed in the struggle.

359
00:36:17.049 --> 00:36:20.218
Seven of your best men killed by women?

360
00:36:22.471 --> 00:36:25.390
I wish to know where
the Epirus Bow rests.

361
00:36:29.937 --> 00:36:31.646
Which of you can tell me this?

362
00:36:34.901 --> 00:36:37.402
Which of you are the true oracle?

363
00:36:44.202 --> 00:36:46.661
If I'm forced to sort you out
by other means

364
00:36:46.829 --> 00:36:49.623
you will experience discomfort.

365
00:36:50.374 --> 00:36:53.251
Discomfort unique to your gender.

366
00:36:54.795 --> 00:36:58.423
So you tell me, which one of you is her?

367
00:37:01.219 --> 00:37:02.969
I am the one you seek.

368
00:37:04.555 --> 00:37:05.847
No, it is I.

369
00:37:07.058 --> 00:37:08.683
I am the one you seek.

370
00:37:10.645 --> 00:37:14.397
The other one said the same thing.
They all claim to be the oracle.

371
00:37:14.565 --> 00:37:15.899
The other one?

372
00:37:17.235 --> 00:37:18.568
Yes, my king.

373
00:37:19.445 --> 00:37:21.071
The other one? What other one?

374
00:37:21.239 --> 00:37:22.906
There were four of them.

375
00:37:24.700 --> 00:37:25.825
One of them escaped.

376
00:37:27.245 --> 00:37:30.038
With a group of slaves
from the watering hole.

377
00:37:41.926 --> 00:37:42.759
(SCREECHES)

378
00:37:43.636 --> 00:37:46.096
- HYPERION: Mondragon.
- Sire.

379
00:37:46.264 --> 00:37:48.265
Find the one that escaped.

380
00:37:48.432 --> 00:37:49.641
Bring her to me alive.

381
00:38:03.864 --> 00:38:05.198
MAN: The dark seas.

382
00:38:08.119 --> 00:38:09.911
These waters are thick with oiI.

383
00:38:10.788 --> 00:38:14.416
- THESEUS: And the boat?
- It's a Heraklion merchant ship.

384
00:38:15.001 --> 00:38:17.794
Our best bet is to ambush it
and head south.

385
00:38:17.962 --> 00:38:20.922
- South is not ourjourney.
- It is for me.

386
00:38:24.468 --> 00:38:25.802
From what I hear...

387
00:38:26.887 --> 00:38:29.764
...the women down there can get
to the meat of a Malaccan chestnut

388
00:38:29.932 --> 00:38:31.349
with only their tongues.

389
00:38:34.979 --> 00:38:38.148
Shall you and I test the limits
of that desire, my dear?

390
00:38:40.568 --> 00:38:45.447
The gods have given me vision. Yet all
you do is dream of your appetites.

391
00:38:45.614 --> 00:38:49.159
I'd rather follow my appetites
than the hallucinations of a harlot.

392
00:38:49.327 --> 00:38:52.162
- She's a high priestess.
- It doesn't matter to me.

393
00:38:52.330 --> 00:38:54.581
High priestess or whore,
I'm heading south.

394
00:38:54.999 --> 00:38:56.833
(GRUNTING)

395
00:39:01.047 --> 00:39:03.131
Was it something I said?

396
00:39:04.633 --> 00:39:07.093
Well, friend, what will it be?

397
00:39:07.636 --> 00:39:11.848
South with me, or will you follow...

398
00:39:13.684 --> 00:39:15.018
...the lady?

399
00:39:15.686 --> 00:39:17.020
Neither.

400
00:39:19.815 --> 00:39:23.693
I'm taking that ship north,
to Hyperion's camp at the monastery.

401
00:39:26.280 --> 00:39:29.866
Your savior sounds a lot
like a madman to me, Your Highness.

402
00:39:32.036 --> 00:39:36.539
Personally, I'd rather fight
with a madman than against one.

403
00:40:08.072 --> 00:40:09.447
Are you minding this?

404
00:40:13.494 --> 00:40:16.538
That is the mortaI
your father so extols, is it not?

405
00:40:23.003 --> 00:40:24.796
And he is with the oracle.

406
00:40:24.964 --> 00:40:29.217
Poseidon, if Zeus were to suspect you,
we will come to your defense.

407
00:40:37.393 --> 00:40:38.810
(GRUNTING)

408
00:40:46.569 --> 00:40:47.569
The rear!

409
00:40:49.447 --> 00:40:50.613
(SHOUTING)

410
00:40:50.781 --> 00:40:52.407
I thought you said
this was a merchant ship!

411
00:40:54.285 --> 00:40:55.577
I guess I was wrong.

412
00:40:55.744 --> 00:40:58.788
The sea has forever been
an unpredictable domain.

413
00:41:12.761 --> 00:41:14.262
(SHOUTING)

414
00:41:19.393 --> 00:41:23.313
When the cloudless skies thunder...
stand fast.

415
00:41:24.982 --> 00:41:27.525
- We gotta jump now!
- Stand fast!

416
00:41:45.252 --> 00:41:46.544
(SCREAMS)

417
00:41:49.548 --> 00:41:53.009
(SHOUTS)

418
00:42:51.193 --> 00:42:52.735
You knew that wave would save us.

419
00:42:57.241 --> 00:43:01.995
What I see is only a glimmer
ofwhat may come to pass.

420
00:43:03.581 --> 00:43:06.583
Your actions and desires
shape what lies ahead.

421
00:43:09.962 --> 00:43:11.462
What else have you seen?

422
00:43:16.760 --> 00:43:19.929
A body wrapped in a shroud on a rock.

423
00:43:21.015 --> 00:43:23.099
You holding the Epirus Bow...

424
00:43:24.685 --> 00:43:26.144
...and...

425
00:43:30.107 --> 00:43:33.109
- ... embracing Hyperion.
- Impossible.

426
00:43:33.277 --> 00:43:35.737
I would never embrace Hyperion.

427
00:43:36.780 --> 00:43:38.114
He killed my mother.

428
00:43:39.825 --> 00:43:41.075
Your mother.

429
00:43:42.453 --> 00:43:44.495
Was she given a proper buriaI?

430
00:43:47.458 --> 00:43:48.625
No.

431
00:43:49.460 --> 00:43:52.337
She still lies
where Hyperion cut her down.

432
00:43:53.380 --> 00:43:57.258
Then you must bury your mother.
Her faith demands it.

433
00:43:58.010 --> 00:43:59.594
I do not believe in the gods.

434
00:44:00.179 --> 00:44:01.596
But she believed.

435
00:44:03.349 --> 00:44:06.184
She believed, Theseus.

436
00:44:07.227 --> 00:44:09.145
You must return to your village.

437
00:44:11.065 --> 00:44:13.816
(DISTANT SHOUTING)

438
00:44:19.990 --> 00:44:21.908
(DOG SNARLS)

439
00:44:31.168 --> 00:44:33.211
Have you found the oracle?

440
00:44:33.379 --> 00:44:37.173
We did, my Lord, but our men were lost
before we could recover her.

441
00:44:37.341 --> 00:44:39.509
A storm swept them to sea.

442
00:44:40.969 --> 00:44:42.303
And the oracle.

443
00:44:43.931 --> 00:44:45.515
Did she survive?

444
00:44:45.683 --> 00:44:48.393
She travels towards Kolpos
with the slaves.

445
00:44:48.894 --> 00:44:50.895
She could be leading them to the Bow.

446
00:44:55.025 --> 00:44:56.067
Mm.

447
00:44:59.029 --> 00:45:03.574
Send the Beast to Kolpos.
We will go to Tartarus.

448
00:45:04.702 --> 00:45:06.369
- Mondragon?
- Sire.

449
00:45:07.037 --> 00:45:11.708
HYPERION: You stay here...
and set an ambush in the pit.

450
00:45:11.875 --> 00:45:14.419
(INDISTINCT SHOUTING)

451
00:45:15.003 --> 00:45:17.213
(WAVES CRASHING)

452
00:45:52.124 --> 00:45:55.001
(BIRDS CALLING)

453
00:45:57.254 --> 00:45:59.922
(WIND HOWLING)

454
00:46:34.833 --> 00:46:36.626
(STONES GRINDING)

455
00:46:42.132 --> 00:46:44.300
I'm sorry I couldn't
protect you, Mother.

456
00:46:49.890 --> 00:46:52.809
But I promise you our family name
will not die with me.

457
00:46:55.979 --> 00:46:57.980
- (GRUNTS)
- (STONES CONTINUE GRINDING)

458
00:47:17.960 --> 00:47:20.670
(INDISTINCT WHISPERS)

459
00:48:52.429 --> 00:48:53.763
(RUSTLING)

460
00:49:14.284 --> 00:49:15.576
(GASPS)

461
00:49:28.382 --> 00:49:30.132
(ROARING)

462
00:49:46.149 --> 00:49:47.316
(SNARLS)

463
00:49:47.943 --> 00:49:50.486
(BOTH GRUNTING)

464
00:50:07.629 --> 00:50:08.671
(CRIES OUT)

465
00:50:12.467 --> 00:50:13.175
(SNARLS)

466
00:50:13.343 --> 00:50:14.969
(BOTH GRUNTING)

467
00:50:28.525 --> 00:50:30.651
(PANTING)

468
00:50:51.214 --> 00:50:52.798
(GROANS)

469
00:50:54.009 --> 00:50:55.051
(SHOUTS)

470
00:51:08.231 --> 00:51:10.399
(PANTING)

471
00:51:10.859 --> 00:51:11.984
(GRUNTING)

472
00:51:28.752 --> 00:51:30.961
(PANTING)

473
00:51:33.590 --> 00:51:35.758
(LOW GROWLING)

474
00:51:48.772 --> 00:51:51.273
MAN: Hyperion's legions
are gathering at Tartarus.

475
00:51:52.609 --> 00:51:54.485
That's where Hellenes will fall.

476
00:51:55.862 --> 00:51:57.279
That future is not set.

477
00:51:58.949 --> 00:52:02.284
But likely. It will be a slaughter.

478
00:52:03.787 --> 00:52:06.789
- You have no faith.
- Heathens.

479
00:52:08.375 --> 00:52:12.419
That is true, Dareios, but not always.

480
00:52:13.004 --> 00:52:17.675
When I was just a boy,
I prayed to the gods... for a horse.

481
00:52:17.843 --> 00:52:22.471
The gods never answered me,
so I stole one instead.

482
00:52:23.640 --> 00:52:25.474
(DAREIOS PANTING)

483
00:52:27.811 --> 00:52:29.728
We're surrounded by heathens.

484
00:52:33.817 --> 00:52:35.568
(SWORDS UNSHEATHING)

485
00:52:36.736 --> 00:52:39.029
(PANTING)

486
00:52:42.993 --> 00:52:44.827
(SHOUTING)

487
00:53:38.256 --> 00:53:40.007
(BIRD SCREECHING)

488
00:53:48.225 --> 00:53:49.642
(GRUNTS)

489
00:54:07.077 --> 00:54:08.369
(GROANS)

490
00:54:10.080 --> 00:54:13.249
It's all right. It's all right, Theseus.

491
00:54:15.543 --> 00:54:17.169
What happened to me?

492
00:54:17.337 --> 00:54:20.256
Your arm. You were poisoned.

493
00:54:26.429 --> 00:54:28.055
Where are the others?

494
00:54:29.057 --> 00:54:31.725
They're putting Dareios' body to rest.

495
00:54:50.662 --> 00:54:51.996
She was right.

496
00:54:56.042 --> 00:54:57.960
For all those years, I doubted her.

497
00:55:00.463 --> 00:55:03.924
Doubted their existence.

498
00:55:05.969 --> 00:55:08.971
Your mother's death
was not in vain, Theseus.

499
00:55:11.308 --> 00:55:15.477
It was fate that brought you back.
For the Bow.

500
00:55:19.941 --> 00:55:22.484
And in your hands, Theseus...

501
00:55:23.987 --> 00:55:26.071
...it will bring Hellenes victory.

502
00:57:03.211 --> 00:57:07.548
You were right, Theseus.
My visions are a curse.

503
00:57:08.466 --> 00:57:11.093
I want to see the world
through my own eyes.

504
00:57:12.637 --> 00:57:15.180
And feel with my own heart.

505
00:57:15.807 --> 00:57:17.891
And touch with my own flesh.

506
00:57:34.659 --> 00:57:38.537
Hey, monk, I did a little shopping
last night. Good weapon, huh?

507
00:57:52.635 --> 00:57:54.470
Good to you see you're still alive.

508
00:57:54.971 --> 00:57:57.556
I was worried that cow
had gotten the best of you.

509
00:57:58.308 --> 00:58:01.351
It almost did. She saved my life.

510
00:58:04.063 --> 00:58:05.647
Looks like she did more than that.

511
00:58:10.069 --> 00:58:11.069
CarefuI.

512
00:58:12.155 --> 00:58:15.491
Just because you have that bow doesn't
mean I'm going to treat you differently.

513
00:58:16.159 --> 00:58:18.785
Good. We march to the monastery.

514
00:58:20.997 --> 00:58:22.331
We have a war to fight.

515
00:58:26.836 --> 00:58:31.423
LYSANDER: The faithfuI believe the Titans
are still buried deep within the mountain.

516
00:58:37.263 --> 00:58:41.642
The Great Wall is the Hellenics'
only hope against your army.

517
00:58:48.900 --> 00:58:50.067
Defenses?

518
00:58:50.235 --> 00:58:54.738
Originally it was a dam,
but the Hellenics have since adapted it.

519
00:58:57.075 --> 00:59:00.744
No one could have anticipated the enemy
you have become.

520
00:59:01.663 --> 00:59:02.996
How many are there?

521
00:59:03.665 --> 00:59:06.708
How many have made it here,
Your Majesty, I'm not sure.

522
00:59:06.876 --> 00:59:08.043
How many?

523
00:59:08.795 --> 00:59:10.462
I'm not sure, Your Majesty.

524
00:59:12.799 --> 00:59:15.634
- Eight hundred.
- And the gate?

525
00:59:15.802 --> 00:59:20.138
Twenty feet of marble stone,
weighing over 12 tons.

526
00:59:20.306 --> 00:59:23.559
It was designed to be impenetrable,
Your Majesty.

527
00:59:25.311 --> 00:59:31.149
Have you ever known of a gate
designed to be anything but?

528
00:59:41.661 --> 00:59:43.453
Go be of service somewhere else.

529
00:59:56.843 --> 00:59:59.511
(EERIE HOWLING SOUNDS)

530
01:00:01.514 --> 01:00:05.517
Where is he? I thought Hyperion
was supposed to be camped here.

531
01:00:05.685 --> 01:00:10.480
We should continue. Tartarus is another
two days along this ridge.

532
01:00:11.816 --> 01:00:13.150
What is that sound?

533
01:00:33.296 --> 01:00:36.214
(MUFFLED SCREAMING)

534
01:00:36.633 --> 01:00:38.091
(MAN SHOUTING)

535
01:00:43.806 --> 01:00:46.308
Stay down, monk! Stavros, help me!

536
01:00:47.310 --> 01:00:48.810
Help me keep him down!

537
01:00:52.357 --> 01:00:54.608
No! No!

538
01:00:56.152 --> 01:00:59.821
My sisters! My sisters!

539
01:01:00.615 --> 01:01:02.157
STAVROS: They're in the bull!

540
01:01:08.790 --> 01:01:09.790
No!

541
01:01:16.506 --> 01:01:17.798
(SOBBING)

542
01:01:24.514 --> 01:01:26.640
- I am the true oracle.
- It's me, Phaedra!

543
01:01:26.808 --> 01:01:28.266
I am the oracle.

544
01:01:31.437 --> 01:01:32.521
Theseus.

545
01:01:33.272 --> 01:01:34.648
They're still here.

546
01:01:37.652 --> 01:01:39.403
(SHOUTS ANGRILY)

547
01:01:41.280 --> 01:01:42.406
Wait, monk!

548
01:01:44.534 --> 01:01:45.867
It's a trap!

549
01:01:51.124 --> 01:01:53.709
(SCREAMING)

550
01:01:53.876 --> 01:01:56.044
(PANTING)

551
01:02:01.134 --> 01:02:03.009
- Monk!
- (SNARLING)

552
01:02:03.636 --> 01:02:06.096
(ALL GRUNTING)

553
01:02:11.477 --> 01:02:12.561
(SNARLING)

554
01:02:18.568 --> 01:02:19.901
(GRUNTS)

555
01:02:20.069 --> 01:02:21.403
Theseus.

556
01:02:27.243 --> 01:02:28.785
(GRUNTS)

557
01:02:28.953 --> 01:02:30.162
(SHOUTS)

558
01:02:34.208 --> 01:02:36.918
(GRUNTING)

559
01:03:00.318 --> 01:03:02.068
(HORSES WHINNY)

560
01:03:07.450 --> 01:03:09.618
Do not stop untiI you reach Tartarus.

561
01:03:09.786 --> 01:03:11.953
The horses will run
untiI their hearts give out.

562
01:03:12.121 --> 01:03:15.207
Hyperion will soon have the Bow. Leave.

563
01:03:30.765 --> 01:03:32.432
(PANTING)

564
01:03:37.730 --> 01:03:39.689
(FOOTSTEPS RUMBLING)

565
01:03:41.818 --> 01:03:44.611
Forgive me, Father. Forgive me.

566
01:03:46.280 --> 01:03:48.824
I only broke the law
to protect the mortaI.

567
01:04:00.670 --> 01:04:03.964
(SLOW-MOTION SHOUT)

568
01:04:30.199 --> 01:04:33.368
No god will ever again come to your aid.

569
01:04:34.704 --> 01:04:36.371
You are on your own!

570
01:04:39.041 --> 01:04:41.710
Do you understand, mortaI?

571
01:04:42.879 --> 01:04:45.297
I have faith in you, Theseus.

572
01:04:46.048 --> 01:04:49.926
Prove me right.

573
01:04:50.553 --> 01:04:52.053
Lead your people.

574
01:05:03.900 --> 01:05:05.609
(SCREECHING)

575
01:05:34.138 --> 01:05:35.263
Halt!

576
01:05:36.724 --> 01:05:39.017
(HORSES SNORTING, PANTING)

577
01:05:46.192 --> 01:05:47.651
(SNARLING)

578
01:05:52.406 --> 01:05:54.366
The horse I prayed for when I was a boy.

579
01:05:55.034 --> 01:05:56.201
What is wrong with him?

580
01:05:58.996 --> 01:06:00.121
They're dying.

581
01:06:21.978 --> 01:06:23.979
Where are the men?

582
01:06:24.146 --> 01:06:26.231
MAN: They have yet to return, sire.

583
01:06:27.108 --> 01:06:29.442
What does the sight
of the bird tell you?

584
01:06:32.655 --> 01:06:33.655
Speak.

585
01:06:36.534 --> 01:06:37.659
The gods.

586
01:06:40.079 --> 01:06:41.871
They came from above.

587
01:06:42.498 --> 01:06:43.915
The gods?

588
01:06:44.083 --> 01:06:46.710
They appeared and laid waste
to the men, my king.

589
01:06:49.463 --> 01:06:50.714
The gods.

590
01:06:53.592 --> 01:06:54.843
The gods.

591
01:06:55.886 --> 01:06:58.972
They protected the slave
who travels with the oracle.

592
01:07:02.518 --> 01:07:05.353
The gods fight on their behalf, sire.

593
01:07:10.693 --> 01:07:13.194
If the men hear of this,
there will be panic.

594
01:07:14.363 --> 01:07:17.115
I know. I know.

595
01:07:19.535 --> 01:07:20.952
(SQUISHING)

596
01:07:21.120 --> 01:07:23.204
(SCREAMING CONTINUES)

597
01:08:05.331 --> 01:08:08.458
ATHENA: In peace, sons bury their fathers.

598
01:08:09.919 --> 01:08:13.379
In war, fathers bury their sons.

599
01:08:21.180 --> 01:08:22.972
Are we at war, Father?

600
01:08:50.876 --> 01:08:52.919
(INDISTINCT CHATTERING)

601
01:09:04.181 --> 01:09:06.099
I have important information
for the counciI.

602
01:09:06.267 --> 01:09:07.433
Theseus.

603
01:09:08.060 --> 01:09:09.769
I know this man. Let him through.

604
01:09:15.943 --> 01:09:17.777
I hope you've come to join the fight.

605
01:09:30.916 --> 01:09:32.250
Where's the army?

606
01:09:42.261 --> 01:09:44.012
Tell me about the slave.

607
01:09:47.183 --> 01:09:49.350
He's from your village, is he not?

608
01:09:51.187 --> 01:09:53.021
- Answer me!
- Yes.

609
01:09:54.523 --> 01:09:56.357
He was a peasant.

610
01:10:00.696 --> 01:10:02.447
As was I.

611
01:10:03.449 --> 01:10:05.366
Forgive me, Your Majesty.

612
01:10:05.534 --> 01:10:07.744
- I meant no...
- Quiet.

613
01:10:07.912 --> 01:10:10.246
And his family?

614
01:10:10.414 --> 01:10:14.834
His mother was raped by some villagers.
Nobody would marry her.

615
01:10:17.463 --> 01:10:18.880
He was a bastard.

616
01:10:19.048 --> 01:10:21.049
(THUNDER RUMBLES)

617
01:10:23.385 --> 01:10:24.719
And his name?

618
01:10:25.596 --> 01:10:26.721
Theseus.

619
01:10:27.723 --> 01:10:29.891
Very well. I'll meet him.

620
01:10:40.319 --> 01:10:43.238
Helios tells me you have information
that could be of use to us.

621
01:10:43.405 --> 01:10:45.698
Hyperion is in possession
of the Epirus Bow.

622
01:10:47.243 --> 01:10:49.702
- The Epirus Bow?
- Yes, it's a weapon forged by Heracles.

623
01:10:49.870 --> 01:10:52.497
Oh, please. I heard the same stories
you did as a child.

624
01:10:52.665 --> 01:10:56.960
There are gods living in the clouds.
Titans buried in the rocks.

625
01:10:57.127 --> 01:11:02.090
Listen, I was a disbelieverjust like
you are. But the Epirus Bow exists.

626
01:11:02.258 --> 01:11:07.428
I understand there are many Hellenics
who put faith in the myths and the gods,

627
01:11:07.596 --> 01:11:10.306
but we on the Hellenic counciI do not.

628
01:11:10.474 --> 01:11:13.309
They are metaphors, son. Nothing more.

629
01:11:13.477 --> 01:11:17.355
We are a society of laws
based on negotiation and reason.

630
01:11:17.523 --> 01:11:20.775
If you try and negotiate with Hyperion,
you will be the death of us all.

631
01:11:20.943 --> 01:11:23.903
If I were to accept your counseI,

632
01:11:24.071 --> 01:11:26.656
Theseus from Kolpos, what would it be?

633
01:11:26.824 --> 01:11:29.325
SeaI the gates and prepare for war.

634
01:11:29.493 --> 01:11:31.619
We have Hoplite battalions returning.
We can't seaI the gate.

635
01:11:31.787 --> 01:11:35.665
No one will return! We are the last!

636
01:11:35.833 --> 01:11:38.167
I'm sure you'll understand
if I don't accept the advice

637
01:11:38.335 --> 01:11:41.671
of an alluring palm reader
and her peasant lover.

638
01:11:43.340 --> 01:11:45.508
Sir, a Heraklion envoy approaches.

639
01:11:49.054 --> 01:11:53.308
There, you see? No ruler wishes for war.

640
01:11:53.475 --> 01:11:57.395
They only wish to be taken seriously
at the bargaining table.

641
01:11:58.230 --> 01:12:00.648
Alert the council. Prepare a delegation.

642
01:12:04.903 --> 01:12:05.987
MAN: Bows!

643
01:12:10.200 --> 01:12:11.200
HELIOS: Stop!

644
01:12:14.330 --> 01:12:18.750
Stop! Remain still,
or we'll be forced to fire upon you.

645
01:12:22.963 --> 01:12:24.672
Extend your arms outward.

646
01:12:28.552 --> 01:12:30.553
He bears the olive branch of peace.

647
01:12:31.889 --> 01:12:36.559
HYPERION: My king wishes to speak
to the one called Theseus from Kolpos.

648
01:12:40.856 --> 01:12:42.190
Theseus.

649
01:12:44.693 --> 01:12:47.278
Hyperion's envoy
desires a word with you.

650
01:12:48.739 --> 01:12:52.575
Like the vision,
he sends for you with arms open.

651
01:12:54.078 --> 01:12:56.162
Seeking an embrace of loyalty.

652
01:12:56.330 --> 01:12:57.997
Phaedra.

653
01:12:59.208 --> 01:13:00.917
Have you never been wrong?

654
01:13:14.223 --> 01:13:15.932
We can't protect you beyond this gate.

655
01:13:23.065 --> 01:13:24.732
I am Theseus!

656
01:13:25.234 --> 01:13:28.236
Come closer. I have a message for you.

657
01:13:29.196 --> 01:13:30.238
Don't risk it.

658
01:13:35.077 --> 01:13:36.661
At worst, you lose a peasant.

659
01:13:46.922 --> 01:13:49.549
- Better?
- Uh-huh. Yes.

660
01:13:51.176 --> 01:13:53.094
Why do you cover your face?

661
01:13:53.262 --> 01:13:55.972
All are equal in Hyperion's midst.

662
01:13:56.140 --> 01:13:59.434
I myself am only a vesseI
for his demands. Nothing more.

663
01:14:00.561 --> 01:14:03.980
- And he asks me by name?
- Indeed he does.

664
01:14:04.148 --> 01:14:05.523
And how does he know it?

665
01:14:05.691 --> 01:14:08.401
There's little the king does not know.

666
01:14:08.569 --> 01:14:10.736
He knows that you have no father.

667
01:14:10.904 --> 01:14:14.115
And like him, you were cast aside
by your own people.

668
01:14:14.283 --> 01:14:15.950
Does he know of my rage?

669
01:14:17.411 --> 01:14:20.788
Does he know that I live only to see
his blood at the end of my sword?

670
01:14:20.956 --> 01:14:22.957
Does he know he butchered my mother?

671
01:14:31.133 --> 01:14:35.261
Now that he's seen your face, he knows.

672
01:14:44.646 --> 01:14:45.980
You wouldn't make it.

673
01:14:47.232 --> 01:14:48.649
Coward!

674
01:14:48.817 --> 01:14:50.651
Embrace me, Theseus.

675
01:14:51.778 --> 01:14:54.822
They will never give you a seat
at their table

676
01:14:54.990 --> 01:14:56.741
but you could sit at the head of mine.

677
01:14:58.160 --> 01:15:03.372
Long after this war is over, my mark
will be left on this world forever.

678
01:15:05.959 --> 01:15:09.587
The sun will never set
on my blood, Theseus.

679
01:15:09.755 --> 01:15:13.424
This is what I offer you. Immortality.

680
01:15:14.593 --> 01:15:17.845
Deeds are eternaI. Not the flesh.

681
01:15:22.643 --> 01:15:25.811
The gods may be on your side,
but tomorrow...

682
01:15:27.147 --> 01:15:28.856
...I unleash the Titans.

683
01:15:33.529 --> 01:15:35.029
What was discussed?

684
01:15:36.031 --> 01:15:37.865
SeaI the gate.

685
01:15:38.033 --> 01:15:41.118
- What were his demands?
- SeaI the gate.

686
01:15:42.287 --> 01:15:43.871
HYPERION: Theseus.

687
01:15:46.375 --> 01:15:48.167
Ahh...

688
01:15:50.128 --> 01:15:51.629
(SHOUTS)

689
01:16:00.514 --> 01:16:03.516
(INDISTINCT CHATTERING)

690
01:16:10.315 --> 01:16:13.442
- That was him, wasn't it?
- I was that close.

691
01:16:45.392 --> 01:16:48.269
I don't know if I can do
what Zeus asks of me.

692
01:16:51.940 --> 01:16:54.317
By doubting one
comes the truth, Theseus.

693
01:16:59.114 --> 01:17:00.573
The gods chose well.

694
01:18:49.182 --> 01:18:52.268
Sir, there's movement on the front.

695
01:19:16.001 --> 01:19:17.668
What is he holding?

696
01:19:20.922 --> 01:19:21.964
The Bow.

697
01:19:38.982 --> 01:19:42.109
MAN: The commanders
are all dead! Fall back!

698
01:19:42.277 --> 01:19:43.861
(PANICKED SHOUTING)

699
01:19:49.117 --> 01:19:51.035
Hold! Stand your ground!

700
01:19:51.620 --> 01:19:54.038
Hold! Stand your ground!

701
01:20:06.760 --> 01:20:08.093
Listen to me!

702
01:20:11.598 --> 01:20:12.765
Listen!

703
01:20:16.144 --> 01:20:20.231
- Who are you to tell us what to do?
- I am nobody to tell you what to do!

704
01:20:20.398 --> 01:20:23.776
I am Theseus, a common man! One of you!

705
01:20:23.944 --> 01:20:27.446
I share your blood!
And I share your fear!

706
01:20:28.323 --> 01:20:33.452
But to run now would offer our souls
and the souls of our children

707
01:20:33.620 --> 01:20:35.329
to a terrible darkness!

708
01:20:38.875 --> 01:20:41.001
(ALL SHOUTING)

709
01:20:45.090 --> 01:20:47.925
Hold! We must stand and fight!

710
01:20:48.468 --> 01:20:52.263
Their numbers count for nothing
in the tunneI! Stand your ground!

711
01:20:54.599 --> 01:20:57.852
Stand your ground!
Who are they that we are not?

712
01:21:00.522 --> 01:21:03.983
Just because they scald their faces
and scar their bodies...

713
01:21:04.734 --> 01:21:08.279
...does not mean they are braver
or stronger than we are.

714
01:21:08.989 --> 01:21:10.239
They are cowards!

715
01:21:11.116 --> 01:21:12.616
They hide behind their masks.

716
01:21:13.326 --> 01:21:17.079
They are human,
and they bleed like you and I.

717
01:21:23.461 --> 01:21:24.795
Listen to me!

718
01:21:25.881 --> 01:21:27.339
Stand your ground!

719
01:21:28.216 --> 01:21:30.050
Fight for honor!

720
01:21:30.218 --> 01:21:31.886
Fight for the man beside you!

721
01:21:32.053 --> 01:21:34.346
Fight for the mothers who bore you!

722
01:21:34.514 --> 01:21:36.056
Fight for your children!

723
01:21:36.224 --> 01:21:37.641
Fight for your future!

724
01:21:38.351 --> 01:21:39.894
Fight so your name survives!

725
01:21:41.396 --> 01:21:42.354
Fight...

726
01:21:43.315 --> 01:21:45.232
...for immortality!

727
01:21:52.324 --> 01:21:55.367
Let us write history
with Heraklion blood!

728
01:21:57.329 --> 01:21:59.330
(FOOTSTEPS RUMBLING)

729
01:22:03.376 --> 01:22:06.086
Ready! Move!

730
01:22:41.122 --> 01:22:41.956
(SHOUTS)

731
01:22:51.132 --> 01:22:53.842
(ALL GRUNTING, SHOUTING)

732
01:23:29.546 --> 01:23:31.338
King Hyperion.

733
01:23:32.757 --> 01:23:36.093
We can negotiate. I see no reason...

734
01:23:46.354 --> 01:23:48.355
HYPERION: Theseus!

735
01:23:49.441 --> 01:23:52.776
Here I am! Theseus of Kolpos!

736
01:23:56.489 --> 01:23:58.699
- Where's your king?
- He is no king.

737
01:24:16.509 --> 01:24:17.217
(SHOUTS)

738
01:24:20.555 --> 01:24:21.764
Stavros! The shrine!

739
01:24:45.830 --> 01:24:47.956
Theseus! I'm right behind you!

740
01:25:05.266 --> 01:25:06.600
Phaedra!

741
01:25:09.562 --> 01:25:11.230
Phaedra!

742
01:25:11.397 --> 01:25:12.731
Stay in the shrine.

743
01:25:44.806 --> 01:25:45.973
Hyperion!

744
01:25:53.606 --> 01:25:55.315
(SNARLING)

745
01:25:58.069 --> 01:25:59.153
No!

746
01:26:21.259 --> 01:26:22.843
(GRUNTS)

747
01:26:23.011 --> 01:26:24.344
STAVROS (MUFFLED):
Theseus, wake up!

748
01:26:30.101 --> 01:26:31.393
Theseus!

749
01:26:34.981 --> 01:26:36.273
Theseus!

750
01:26:46.117 --> 01:26:47.534
(GROANS)

751
01:26:57.128 --> 01:26:58.378
Theseus!

752
01:26:59.964 --> 01:27:01.298
I got the Bow!

753
01:27:02.217 --> 01:27:03.675
Stavros.

754
01:27:05.386 --> 01:27:08.138
I got the Bow.
Get out of here while you can!

755
01:27:10.141 --> 01:27:11.183
I'll hold them off!

756
01:27:11.351 --> 01:27:12.517
Stavros.

757
01:27:12.685 --> 01:27:15.729
Go now! I got the Bow!

758
01:27:15.897 --> 01:27:17.356
I'll hold them offwhile I can!

759
01:27:17.523 --> 01:27:20.525
- Get out of here! Go!
- (CREATURES SNARLING)

760
01:27:25.573 --> 01:27:27.741
Which one of you are coming with me?

761
01:27:34.082 --> 01:27:36.083
(SCREAMING)

762
01:27:57.939 --> 01:28:00.357
None of you will leave this place.

763
01:28:02.235 --> 01:28:04.152
(SHOUTS)

764
01:28:15.206 --> 01:28:16.456
Leave here!

765
01:28:17.625 --> 01:28:19.584
This is no longer your fight.

766
01:28:21.796 --> 01:28:23.130
Find Hyperion.

767
01:28:27.302 --> 01:28:29.886
(ALL SNARLING)

768
01:28:34.392 --> 01:28:37.227
(GODS GRUNTING)

769
01:28:56.622 --> 01:28:57.497
(GASPS)

770
01:29:06.883 --> 01:29:08.633
(GRUNTING)

771
01:29:10.845 --> 01:29:13.430
(BOTH SCREAMING)

772
01:29:14.974 --> 01:29:16.808
(BOTH GRUNTING)

773
01:29:45.213 --> 01:29:46.755
(GROANING)

774
01:29:47.882 --> 01:29:50.050
(PANTING)

775
01:29:59.602 --> 01:30:01.269
Die with your gods.

776
01:30:11.239 --> 01:30:13.281
(BOTH SHOUTING)

777
01:30:37.932 --> 01:30:39.641
(SNARLING)

778
01:30:45.189 --> 01:30:47.065
(BREATHING HEAVILY)

779
01:31:10.965 --> 01:31:13.258
(BREATHING HEAVILY)

780
01:31:18.347 --> 01:31:19.723
(GRUNTING)

781
01:31:23.978 --> 01:31:26.271
(SHOUTING)

782
01:31:33.237 --> 01:31:35.530
(ALL SHOUTING)

783
01:31:50.671 --> 01:31:52.172
(SHOUTING)

784
01:32:18.658 --> 01:32:20.075
Athena!

785
01:32:30.336 --> 01:32:32.170
(GROANING)

786
01:32:49.855 --> 01:32:50.981
Father!

787
01:32:54.110 --> 01:32:55.944
Don't forsake mankind.

788
01:33:28.603 --> 01:33:29.936
(GRUTNING)

789
01:34:08.976 --> 01:34:10.268
(SIGHS)

790
01:34:19.195 --> 01:34:21.154
What does it feeI like, knowing...

791
01:34:23.157 --> 01:34:25.533
...knowing that there'll
be no memory of you?

792
01:34:27.662 --> 01:34:28.995
I have won.

793
01:34:31.248 --> 01:34:34.668
My death will make me a legend.

794
01:34:34.835 --> 01:34:36.878
(PANTING)

795
01:34:43.928 --> 01:34:45.261
My deeds...

796
01:34:47.473 --> 01:34:49.724
...will go down in history.

797
01:34:56.273 --> 01:34:58.233
I'm writing your history.

798
01:34:59.276 --> 01:35:00.527
(ROARS)

799
01:35:00.695 --> 01:35:01.611
(SCREAMS)

800
01:35:01.779 --> 01:35:04.072
(BOTH GRUNTING)

801
01:35:17.336 --> 01:35:19.963
(SCREAMING)

802
01:35:25.052 --> 01:35:26.845
Do it!

803
01:35:38.816 --> 01:35:40.525
(MEN SHOUTING)

804
01:35:43.904 --> 01:35:49.617
This... is our last embrace, Hyperion.

805
01:35:52.079 --> 01:35:53.079
Look at me.

806
01:35:55.040 --> 01:35:56.499
Look at me.

807
01:35:58.961 --> 01:36:00.128
I'm the last thing...

808
01:36:01.756 --> 01:36:03.173
...you will ever see.

809
01:36:07.511 --> 01:36:10.972
Witness hell.

810
01:36:11.390 --> 01:36:13.308
(STABBING SOUND)

811
01:36:16.145 --> 01:36:17.812
(GURGLING)

812
01:36:23.277 --> 01:36:25.403
(FADING GROAN)

813
01:37:45.484 --> 01:37:47.777
(ALL SHOUTING)

814
01:38:07.256 --> 01:38:09.090
(SHOUTING, RUMBLING FADES)

815
01:38:32.948 --> 01:38:36.618
OLD MAN: All men's souls are immortal.

816
01:38:39.747 --> 01:38:45.752
But the souls of the righteous
are immortal and divine.

817
01:38:50.257 --> 01:38:52.967
Once a faithless man,

818
01:38:53.135 --> 01:38:57.513
Theseus gave his life to save mankind

819
01:38:57.681 --> 01:39:00.058
and earned a place amongst the gods.

820
01:39:03.312 --> 01:39:06.648
They rewarded his bravery with a gift.

821
01:39:06.815 --> 01:39:10.151
A son. Acamas.

822
01:39:33.050 --> 01:39:34.884
(ARMIES SHOUTING)

823
01:39:35.636 --> 01:39:36.970
(GASPS)

824
01:39:41.809 --> 01:39:44.811
Don't be afraid of your visions,
little one.

825
01:39:46.647 --> 01:39:48.982
- What's your name?
- Acamas.

826
01:39:49.608 --> 01:39:51.317
Acamas.

827
01:39:52.653 --> 01:39:54.612
A strong name.

828
01:39:57.574 --> 01:40:02.161
I knew your father.
He was a very brave man.

829
01:40:05.874 --> 01:40:09.836
Soon, it will be your time.

830
01:40:11.672 --> 01:40:13.214
My time for what?

831
01:40:13.382 --> 01:40:16.259
The fight against eviI
never ends, Acamas.

832
01:40:16.427 --> 01:40:19.220
War is coming to the heavens.

833
01:40:20.639 --> 01:40:25.810
And your father will be there,
fighting for your future.

834
01:40:28.772 --> 01:40:29.772
PHAEDRA: Acamas.

835
01:40:30.441 --> 01:40:31.524
Acamas.

836
01:40:39.867 --> 01:40:41.325
Who was that, son?

837
01:40:42.036 --> 01:40:43.036
Just...

838
01:40:45.706 --> 01:40:47.206
Just an old man.

839
01:41:12.316 --> 01:41:14.650
(BREATHING HEAVILY)

840
01:41:42.429 --> 01:41:44.138
(SNARLING)

841
01:41:47.184 --> 01:41:49.268
(ARMIES SHOUTING)

842
01:41:53.273 --> 01:41:55.775
(GASPS, PANTING)

843
01:50:24.534 --> 01:50:25.534
English - US - PSDH
